  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multi-profile + avgpool (config_002, PCA n2000) is the best result so far (0.591 acc), substantially outperforming single-profile RNA (0.485) and image-only ResNet50 (0.208). Avgpool clearly beats transformer for aggregation (0.591 vs 0.519). However, only PCA n2000 has been tested as an RNA encoder, leaving a major uncertainty: does a learned representation (scVI) improve on the linear PCA baseline in the best-performing multi-profile + avgpool setting? Question: config_005 (RNA-only, multi-profile, scvi_n200, avgpool) isolates the RNA encoder as the single variable changed relative to config_002, directly testing whether a nonlinear learned embedding outperforms PCA. Why this is the best next experiment: Before committing budget to multimodal fusion (which adds image encoder, fusion strategy, and more hyperparameters), we need to know whether the RNA backbone can be improved. If scvi substantially beats PCA here, it reshapes which multimodal configs to prioritize; if it does not, PCA remains the efficient choice and we can focus budget on fusion design. This is a clean, single-variable comparison that maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

